data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":1746,"item_id":"msg_0b2b700f37b18d6b016b099200b6f087d1b759483bb1a348cd","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"kai\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The supplied related-capability search and registry establish observation through probe, qualitative inspection and calibrated readings through examine-material, but no equivalent operation for physically transferring and verifying a length calibration. Reuse those existing functions and their code rather than redeveloping observation or measurement. Develop a general length-reference investigation and transfer operation in the current-conversation handoff. No suitable standard or tool is presently established; its immediately executable result may therefore be a documented physical obstacle, not a calibrated reference. The declared dimensions in construction recipes are not physical standards.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Develop 'Investigate and transfer length references', parameterized by mode (investigate, transfer, verify, resume, cancel), accessible target/reference/carrier item IDs, property, quantity, proposed graduation interval and explicit tools. It is available for any applicable actor to study, not bound to Kai or one specimen. Minimal executable precursor: physically investigate one nominated accessible candidate per action, record observed suitability and provenance or the specific missing prerequisite, and stop honestly when no physical standard exists. Do not invent a search result or fabricate a standard from internal numerical dimensions. Investigation may find an uncalibrated comparison length, but that is explicitly nonmetric and cannot satisfy examine-material's calibration requirement.\\\\nReuse and record dependencies on probe for physical observation, examine-material for applicable inspection/readout checks, consult for reading existing records, and existing travel, pickup and marking operations where actually needed; preserve their contracts and costs, without duplicate charges for the same reused action. Exact existing references are probe (open-baseline:probe:1), examine-material (measurement:material-specimen:nondestructive-examination:1), consult (open-baseline:consult:1), and navigate (base:navigate:1). The handoff must bind shared implementations and record code reuse. Do not treat prepare-ventilated-food-storage's nominal rod dimensions, construct-weather-shelter's recipe, source stock, coordinates, body dimensions or render scale as calibration evidence. Kai's item-24-kai-284 is berries, not a demonstrated measuring tool; canopy-69:unit-1:traits is an incomplete qualitative record, not a length standard. No additional facts may be inferred from its unseen pages.\\\\nStudy costs 2 simulation rounds at 0.2 energy per round, independently per learner. Investigation of one in-reach candidate costs 1 round and 0.2 energy and consumes, reserves and moves no material; inaccessible or nonexistent targets are refused before charging. Ordinary travel and obtaining materials are separate existing actions. Reading a contract alone does not establish a physical fact. Investigation returns a personal evidence record distinguishing observed facts, unsupported claims and unknowns. Report only the scoped conclusion 'no qualifying standard established among these examined candidates', never a global hidden-world search result.\\\\nTransfer requires a physically available, serviceable reference bearing an independently justified length value, unit, uncertainty, resolution, range, provenance and current revision; a whole stable carrier of suitable size; adequate light and access; and an actual method of laying off or comparing lengths. Merely declaring a stick to be one metre is invalid. An arbitrary comparison span may be recorded as such, but is never silently converted to metres or accepted by metric shelter checks. If the registry/world supplies no physically realizable standard, report that obstacle with zero fabrication progress; retain investigation as the useful precursor. Do not introduce an arbitrary era gate or a multistage activity roadmap.\\\\nThe smallest conditional transfer is a single reference span copied onto one already suitable carrier, not an automatic finely graduated ruler. It takes 1 comparison round at 0.2 energy and, if durable endpoint marks are feasible, 1 marking round at 0.2 energy plus any explicit existing marking-tool wear/material cost. The marking mechanism must be physically supported: reuse the existing mark implementation only where its substrate/tool requirements and actual effect suffice; otherwise hand off the missing physical marking mechanism rather than assuming cutting, ink or precision tools. Before commitment, expose the actual carrier, tools, source evidence, required expendables and full costs. No cutting or stock-unit conversion is included. No new material or energy is created: the same carrier acquires only physically performed marks, the reference remains unchanged, and any expendable use or tool wear is deducted exactly once. Investigation never reserves resources; transfer may lock only the named carrier while actively worked, with no ownership transfer or implied permission.\\\\nVerification is a separate completed physical comparison, 1 round and 0.2 energy, against the named valid source using an executable alignment method. Record source and carrier revisions, comparison readings, endpoint placement resolution, repetitions, conditions and a conservative uncertainty that includes source uncertainty and each alignment/mark-placement error; do not assume repeated readings remove systematic error. If placement error cannot be bounded physically, calibration remains unverified. A verified single-span carrier has only that usable span/range and actual resolution; no imaginary subdivisions or diameter support. Publish a serviceable length-calibration record in the exact schema consumed by examine-material, with a traceable evidence chain and supported use conditions. Further spans or subdivisions require individually paid actual work and error propagation, not free scale generation. Existing examine-material restrictions on specimen access, properties, placement uncertainty and stale readings remain unchanged. Calibration cannot bypass shelter checks or establish other material properties.\\\\nTrack completed comparison/mark/verification steps, paid rounds, evidence IDs and actual carrier changes. Pending work advances only on explicit paid actions, never during development/review waiting. Interruption pauses without completing a step; completed physical marks remain but are not a verified calibration. Resume revalidates reference provenance, revisions, tools, access and conditions before accepting previous work; invalidated steps must be redone. Cancel is free, releases locks and retains the carrier in its actual marked/unmarked condition. Death stops work and releases locks; carried objects follow existing death/drop rules, with no duplication or transfer to a reviewer. No spent time, energy, wear or consumed marking material is refunded; untouched inputs remain intact. No autonomous search, fabrication or calibration process runs in the background.\\\\nMaintenance is inspection/reverification after damage, deformation, wear, relevant environmental change or any revision affecting length or marks. Such changes invalidate the calibration immediately; elapsed time alone never repairs it. Reverification uses the same paid verification mode and original physical prerequisites. Real products are evidence records, physically marked existing carriers where feasible, and verified calibration only after completed validation. Implement prerequisite checks, provenance validation, conservation, progress and invalidation in code rather than repeated model review.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":2,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No benefit for requesting, registration, studying, naming or merely issuing investigation queries. A completed observation or comparison may produce verified personally relevant information, including an informative failure identifying the actual missing standard. Route such events through the existing experience system without altering protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions. Deduplicate by actor, physical evidence/revision and functional finding across probe, examine-material and this operation; rereading or repeating an unchanged negative finding adds none. If an existing authorized event category supports it, bound short pleasure to at most one small qualifying event per 10 rounds and maintained satisfaction to a modest cap of 1, subject to the established 0.002-per-round decay and existing global limits; absent such support, award none rather than inventing a reward channel. Legitimate repeated practice can sustain modest benefit only through actual participation under those same caps, not fabricated novelty. No nutrition, shelter protection, comfort or mastery results from records alone; physical comfort remains capped at 10.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit observable investigation, alignment, marking, interruption, verification and failure events only when those actions actually occur. Store reusable metadata: actor, target and source IDs/revisions, mode, physical mark positions only when established, evidence/provenance IDs, work step/progress, calibration state (unknown, comparison-only, pending, verified, stale or failed), supported units/range/resolution/uncertainty and visible condition. Reuse item geometry and appearance; add marks only after physical marking succeeds. Information labels must distinguish private evidence from outwardly visible changes and must not expose hidden dimensions or resources. An unavailable-standard report, incomplete transfer or failed verification must never display a completed ruler, metric ticks, verified badge or shelter-suitability success. No visuals or events imply actions or consent by another participant; any assistance requires their own actual communication and independent actions.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

